her blood pressure, water retention and puffiness, more strain on heart and kidneys over years. Sausages, bread, cheese, soups, sauces and fast food are the big sources.","foods":[["Main sources to watch: sausage and kolbasa","100 g","900-1,200 mg"],["Doner or shawarma","1 wrap","1,200-1,800 mg"],["Instant noodles","1 pack","1,500+ mg"],["Cheese (brynza, feta)","50 g","500-600 mg"],["Bread","2 slices","300-400 mg"],["Lower: cook at home, more herbs, lemon and spices","",""]]},"satFat":{"why":"Saturated fat is the fat that is solid at room temperature: butter, fatty meat, cheese, cream, coconut and palm oil. Some is fine; the 20 g daily figure is a limit.","benefits":["Part of normal food like meat, eggs and dairy, which also bring protein, B12 and calcium"],"low":"Too much over time raises LDL cholesterol and heart-disease risk. Swapping some for olive oil, nuts and fish helps.","foods":[["Watch: butter","1 tbsp (14 g)","7 g"],["Watch: fatty lamb or beef","150 g","8-12 g"],["Watch: cheese","50 g","8-10 g"],["Watch: kazy, sausage","100 g","10-15 g"],["Lower: chicken breast, fish, lean beef","150 g","1-3 g"]]},"omega3":{"why":"Omega-3 fats (EPA and DHA from fish, ALA from plants) are part of every cell membrane, especially in the brain and eyes, and calm inflammation. Your body cannot make enough on its own.","benefits":["Heart health: lower triglycerides","Brain and eye health","Less joint soreness and better recovery from training","Balances diets heavy in seed oils (sunflower oil is mostly omega-6)"],"low":"Too little: dry skin, more inflammation and soreness; over years a higher heart risk. Fish twice a week covers most people.","foods":[["Mackerel (skumbriya)","100 g","2.5 g"],["Herring (seledka)","100 g","1.5-2 g"],["Salmon or trout","100 g","1.5-2 g"],["Canned sardines","100 g","1.4 g"],["Walnuts","30 g","2.5 g (plant form)"],["Flaxseed, ground","1 tbsp","2.3 g (plant form)"],["Eggs (omega-3 enriched)","2 eggs","0.2-0.5 g"]]},"potassium":{"why":"Potassium works with sodium to keep fluid balance, nerve signals and every heartbeat and muscle contraction steady. Most people get too little.","benefits":["Lower blood pressure, especially when salt is high","Fewer muscle cramps","Steady heart rhythm","Better recovery after sweating"],"low":"Too little: cramps, weakness, tiredness, constipation, higher blood pressure. (Very high levels from supplements can be dangerous; food is safe.)","foods":[["Potato, baked with skin","1 medium","900 mg"],["Dried apricots (kuraga)","50 g","600 mg"],["Beans or lentils, cooked","1 cup","700-950 mg"],["Banana","1 medium","420 mg"],["Yogurt or kefir","1 cup","400-550 mg"],["Spinach, cooked","1 cup","840 mg"],["Tomatoes","2 medium","450 mg"],["Salmon","150 g","550 mg"]]},"calcium":{"why":"Calcium builds bones and teeth and is needed for every muscle contraction, nerve signal and blood clotting. If food is short, the body takes it from your bones.","benefits":["Strong bones that resist injury and stress fractures","Normal muscle contraction, including the heart","Works with vitamin D: one without the other is less useful"],"low":"Too little over time: weaker bones (osteoporosis later in life), more stress fractures with hard training, cramps.","foods":[["Kefir or milk","1 glass (250 ml)","300 mg"],["Yogurt","200 g","300-400 mg"],["Hard cheese","30 g","200-250 mg"],["Tvorog (cottage cheese)","150 g","120-180 mg"],["Canned sardines with bones","100 g","380 mg"],["Sesame (tahini)","2 tbsp","130 mg"],["Almonds","30 g","75 mg"],["Broccoli, kale","1 cup cooked","60-180 mg"]]},"iron":{"why":"Iron carries oxygen in your blood (haemoglobin) and muscles (myoglobin). Low iron is one of the most common reasons for feeling tired and weak.","benefits":["Energy and endurance: oxygen reaches the muscles","Focus and memory","Healthy immune system"],"low":"Too little: tiredness, weakness, shortness of breath on stairs, pale skin, feeling cold, poor focus. A blood test (ferritin) is the way to know; do not take iron 