ng. Animal foods give it ready-made; orange and green plants give beta-carotene that the body converts.","benefits":["Night vision and eye health","Healthy skin","Immune defence"],"low":"Too little: poor vision in the dark, dry eyes and skin, more infections. Too much from supplements or liver every day can be harmful; vegetables are safe.","foods":[["Carrot","1 medium","500 µg"],["Sweet potato or pumpkin","1 cup","700-1,000 µg"],["Beef liver","50 g","3,500 µg (once a week is plenty)"],["Spinach, cooked","1 cup","940 µg"],["Eggs","2 large","150 µg"],["Butter","1 tbsp","95 µg"],["Dried apricots","50 g","90 µg"]]},"vitaminC":{"why":"Vitamin C builds collagen (skin, tendons, ligaments, blood vessels), protects cells as an antioxidant, supports the immune system and helps you absorb iron from plant foods. The body cannot store much, so you need it daily.","benefits":["Stronger tendons and joints for training","Immune support","More iron absorbed from plants","Wound and skin healing"],"low":"Too little: easy bruising, bleeding gums, slow healing, tiredness, frequent colds.","foods":[["Red bell pepper","1 medium","150 mg"],["Kiwi","1","64 mg"],["Orange","1","70 mg"],["Rosehip tea","1 cup","varies, can be high"],["Broccoli","1 cup","80 mg"],["Strawberries","1 cup","85 mg"],["Sauerkraut (kvashenaya kapusta)","1 cup","20-35 mg"],["Tomatoes","2 medium","30 mg"]]},"vitaminD":{"why":"Vitamin D lets your body absorb calcium for bones, and supports muscles, immunity and mood. Skin makes it from strong sunlight, but in Kazakhstan from October to March the sun is too low for that, so food (and often a supplement) matters.","benefits":["Strong bones with calcium","Muscle strength and function","Immune defence, fewer winter infections","Mood in the dark months"],"low":"Too little: tiredness, low mood, muscle weakness and aches, frequent illness. Very common in winter. A blood test (25-OH vitamin D) tells you; many doctors suggest 1,000-2,000 IU (25-50 µg) a day in winter.","foods":[[